106
00:13:38.070 --> 00:13:41.030
<v Speaker 1>A seal means the capacity is permanently shut down.

107
00:13:41.830 --> 00:13:47.030
<v Speaker 1>The openings are rendered useless because the individual continually refused to process what was heard and seen.

108
00:13:47.190 --> 00:13:59.510
<v Speaker 2>Third, the instrument is described as covered. In the chapter of the cow, verse 7, the Creator has set a seal on their hearts and on their hearings and on their eyes there is a covering. Theirs will be a great torment.

109
00:13:59.750 --> 00:14:03.590
<v Speaker 1>This implies an obstruction, a self-imposed barrier to reality.

110
00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:13.110
<v Speaker 2>And finally, 4th, it is the mechanism of ultimate accountability. In the chapter of the Children of Israel, verse 36, indeed the hearing, the sight, and the heart of each of those, you will be questioned.

111
00:14:13.190 --> 00:14:19.430
<v Speaker 1>It is the exact same instrument in all four verses, but utilized in four entirely different ways based on human agency.

112
00:14:19.670 --> 00:14:28.710
<v Speaker 2>The critical theological takeaway here is that the error is never the absence of the instrument. The failure is entirely based on what the listener chose to do with it.

113
00:14:29.270 --> 00:14:34.550
<v Speaker 2>The call is heard clearly, the signs are seen vividly, and the true is recognized inwardly.

114
00:14:35.430 --> 00:14:41.990
<v Speaker 1>From that point, they are either accepted and acted upon, or they are ignored, covered, and ultimately sealed by pride.

115
00:14:41.990 --> 00:14:51.190
<v Speaker 2>We are fully equipped. The excuses we often make for our own spiritual stagnation simply do not hold up, because the mechanism for seeking is completely intact.

116
00:14:51.270 --> 00:14:57.590
<v Speaker 1>This connects the argument from the instrument directly to the argument from the messenger. The 2 concepts really cannot be separated.

117
00:14:57.750 --> 00:14:59.150
<v Speaker 2>We see this stitched together

118
00:14:59.230 --> 00:15:13.110
<v Speaker 2>beautifully in the chapter of Women, verse 165, again using the Pictole translation. It states that messengers are sent to bring good cheer and warning so that mankind might have no argument against the Almighty after the messengers.

119
00:15:13.270 --> 00:15:20.230
<v Speaker 1>A demand for obedience is not issued without first providing both the internal means to process it and the external messenger to deliver it.

120
00:15:20.470 --> 00:15:26.630
<v Speaker 2>There are two halves of the same cosmic case. The theological conclusion we arrive at is absolute.

121
00:15:27.510 --> 00:15:33.350
<v Speaker 2>The court of the hereafter is a court in which the defense of ignorance has already been retired before the trial even begins.

122
00:15:33.670 --> 00:15:38.390
<v Speaker 1>In A worldly court, you might successfully claim that you simply did not know the law.

123
00:15:38.790 --> 00:15:49.350
<v Speaker 2>But in the divine court, you cannot claim deprivation when you were handed the instrument of the intellect, and the guides were stationed in the world waiting for your inquiry over in the river country.

124
00:15:49.590 --> 00:15:54.630
<v Speaker 1>The young man in our narrative is standing right at the threshold. He has heard the intricate cosmic design.

125
00:15:55.030 --> 00:16:02.630
<v Speaker 1>He has recognized the gate. He has admitted his own deep neediness by overcoming his hostile lineage, and he has asked for the way to life.

126
00:16:02.950 --> 00:16:20.230
<v Speaker 2>And the master has placed the responsibility squarely back into the young man's own physical and spiritual being. The 3 openings of the human body, hearing, sight, and the heart, perfectly align with the three answering provisions of the relying order, which are the messengers, the imams, and the callers.

127
00:16:20.230 --> 00:16:22.630
<v Speaker 1>The disciple is equipped, and therefore he is accountable.

128
00:16:22.870 --> 00:16:23.510
<v Speaker 2>He is.

129
00:16:24.070 --> 00:16:33.510
<v Speaker 2>And as we conclude our examination of this extraordinary exchange, we are forced to prepare our listener to look at their own standing within this exact same design.

130
00:16:33.590 --> 00:16:36.310
<v Speaker 1>I have no words of my own, for I am following the words of another.

131
00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:45.590
<v Speaker 2>Of the three openings hearing, sight, and the heart, which has gone sealed this week, through what you refuse to inquire about, and what would it cost tomorrow to begin asking?
